# Usually you need none of this.
#
# `npm run dev` proxies /api to Apache automatically (see vite.config.ts), and
# the production build in dist/ calls ../api relative to itself. Both work with
# no configuration as long as Apache serves this project from
# http://localhost/Aurai/aurai-forecast-sim-main/.

# Set this only if Apache serves the project from a different host, port or
# path — it retargets the dev proxy.
# VITE_API_PROXY=http://localhost:8080/my-path/api

# Set this only to bypass the proxy entirely and call the API directly
# (requires the API's CORS headers, which are already permissive).
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost/Aurai/aurai-forecast-sim-main/api

# NOTE: never put an API key in this file or in any VITE_* variable. Vite
# inlines VITE_* values into the built JavaScript, so anyone who opens the app
# can read them. Server-side secrets belong in api/config.local.php, which is
# gitignored — see api/README.md.
